menu "RetroESP32 Platform"

    config BOARD_M5STACK_TAB5
        bool "Target the M5Stack Tab5 (5\" 720x1280 DSI tablet)"
        default n
        help
            Builds for the M5Stack Tab5 instead of the original RetroESP32-P4
            handheld: ILI9881C/ST7123 MIPI-DSI panel (auto-detected), GT911 or
            ST712x touch, ES8388 audio codec, IO-expander power rails and USB-A
            host for gamepads.  The GPIO gamepad is disabled (its pins are used by
            the audio codec).

    config TAB5_DOUBLE_BUFFER
        bool "Tab5: double-buffered, tear-free display"
        default y
        depends on BOARD_M5STACK_TAB5
        help
            Two 720x1280 frame buffers (+1.8 MB PSRAM) swapped at the panel's frame
            boundary, so a picture is never shown half-drawn.  Emulator frames that
            arrive before the previous one reached the screen are dropped rather than
            waited for, so emulation speed never depends on the panel refresh rate.

    config TAB5_ILI9881C_DPI_CLOCK_MHZ
        int "Tab5 v1 (ILI9881C) pixel clock (MHz)"
        default 60
        range 50 80
        depends on BOARD_M5STACK_TAB5
        help
            60 MHz is the M5Stack/esp-bsp setting and refreshes at ~48 Hz, below the
            emulators' 60 FPS.  75 MHz gives ~60 Hz but is outside the tested timing;
            try it if the v1 panel shows judder.

    config TAB5_ST712X_DPI_CLOCK_MHZ
        int "Tab5 v2/v3 (ST7123/ST7121) pixel clock (MHz)"
        default 70
        range 60 80
        depends on BOARD_M5STACK_TAB5
        help
            70 MHz is the esp-bsp setting (~58 Hz).  73 MHz gives ~60 Hz but is
            outside the tested timing.

endmenu
